Template: wwan-manager/lte_iface
Type: string
Default: wwan0
Description: Network interface name of the LTE modem
 The ifupdown interface that is dialed on demand ("ifup wwan0"). Run
 wwan-manager-setup after changing it.

Template: wwan-manager/metric
Type: string
Default: 700
Description: Route metric of the LTE default route
 A higher metric means a lower priority than the primary uplink.

Template: wwan-manager/table
Type: string
Default: 700
Description: Routing table for the LTE routes
 Number of the routing table that gets the LTE routes. Leave empty to use
 the main table.

Template: wwan-manager/dns
Type: string
Default: 1.1.1.1
Description: Name servers to use over LTE
 Space-separated addresses, recorded in /run/wwan/<interface>.dns for
 whatever routes traffic over LTE. Leave empty to use the ones the modem
 hands out.

Template: wwan-manager/at_port
Type: string
Default: /dev/wwan-at
Description: AT control port of the modem
 Normally the udev symlink /dev/wwan-at, which points to the modem's AT
 port.

Template: wwan-manager/qmi_profile
Type: string
Default: 1
Description: Modem profile (PDP context) to dial
 Number of the 3GPP profile whose APN is used. Show or change its APN
 with wwan-apn.

Template: wwan-manager/low_power
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Switch the radio off when LTE is hung up?
 If yes, hanging up also puts the modem into low-power mode (radio off,
 LED off); the next dial switches it on again. If no, the modem stays
 registered on the network.

Template: wwan-manager/ipv6
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Also start an IPv6 session?
 If yes, a second data session gives LTE an IPv6 address, route and name
 servers. The modem's profile must allow IPv6 (PDP type IPV4V6 or IPV6).

Template: wwan-manager/default_route
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Send all internet traffic over LTE while it is up?
 If no, LTE is only a backup route for traffic bound to it. If yes,
 everything without a route of its own moves to LTE while it is up,
 including internal networks that are reached through the primary
 uplink's gateway.
